6. FIND THE BEST PROPOSED DAYS

For every:

Region + Candidate Progress Status

test different Proposed Days values.

The purpose is to find the Proposed Days value that gives the highest probability of correctly predicting the ACTUAL JOINING MONTH.

For every tested Proposed Days value:

Estimated Joining Date =
JR Modified Date + Proposed Days

Then:

Estimated Joining Year-Month =
TEXT(Estimated Joining Date,“yyyymm”)

Compare:

Estimated Joining Year-Month

with:

Actual Joining Year-Month

Create:

Month Correct =
1 when Estimated Joining Year-Month = Actual Joining Year-Month
0 otherwise.

Then calculate:

Month Accuracy % =
SUM(Month Correct) / Number of valid records

The Proposed Days with the highest Month Accuracy % is the candidate optimal Proposed Days.

==================================================
7. PROPOSED DAYS SEARCH RANGE

For each Region + Candidate Progress Status:

First calculate the Median Actual Days to Fill.

Then test Proposed Days around the historical distribution.

Initially test:

Median - 50 days through Median + 50 days.

Do not allow Proposed Days below 0.

If the actual historical distribution extends beyond this range, expand the search range.

The goal is to ensure that the true optimum is not missed.

==================================================
8. IMPORTANT — OPTIMIZE JOINING MONTH, NOT EXACT DATE

The PRIMARY objective is:

Estimated Joining Month = Actual Joining Month

Do NOT optimize primarily for exact joining date.

For example:

JR Modified Date = 31-Mar-2026

Actual Joining Date = 05-Jun-2026

If Proposed Days = 67:

Estimated Joining Date = 06-Jun-2026

This should count as CORRECT because both dates are in June 2026.

Therefore:

Month Accuracy = 100% for this record.

